#
# Which test modules a changed file selects (tools/test-changed reads this). One source glob per line, then the modules it selects.
# `*` stays in one folder, `**` crosses folders, `?` is one character; a module `*` selects the whole suite. A changed path no line
# matches selects the whole suite. A module is tools/test_<name>.py, named test_<name>, or test_selfcheck, which runs
# skills/neckbeard/selfcheck.py. A new tools/test_*.py adds its own `tools/test_X.py test_X` line here, and a line for each source
# file it covers; tools/test_test_parallel.py fails when a module has no row of its own; the reviewer checks the rows for the source files it covers. `make check` and tools/excerpts --check stay outside the herd run.
#
